    <programmerHints>
      <textElement>
        <![CDATA[
          <p>Authentication: the configuration value <i>api_key</i> is exchanged once per connection
          for a session token of limited validity (POST /api/sgr/sgcp/session); reconnect before it
          expires.</p>
          <p>Writing requires the owner's consent (FlexMgmt GetSettings.WriteAccess); without it,
          commands answer 403 and are journalled as rejected, while releases (NORMAL, an inactive
          RestrictPower) are always accepted. Withdrawing the consent ends every command in force
          or pending at the next evaluation cycle.</p>
          <p>OpModeLoadCmd returns the last command; OpLoadState returns the mode actually enforced.
          They differ when MaximumLockTime has elapsed, when a restriction is deferred by
          MinimumRunTime, after 24 h without a new command (fall-back to NORMAL), and while the EMS
          does not apply commands to real devices (observe-only, simulation): the command is then
          recorded, journalled as not_enforceable, and takes effect if the EMS applies again within
          its lock window. The evidence status says which (apply_enabled, not_applying_reason).</p>
          <p>RestrictPower bounds the import at the connection point (MaximumPowerKw), never below the
          declared MinimumLoad; a restriction down at MinimumLoad is a lock and lasts at most
          MaximumLockTime. The feed-in bound (MinimumPowerKw) needs PV control, declared in
          GetSettings.PVControl. MAX is not in force (OpLoadState NORMAL, journalled
          not_enforceable) while a higher-priority signal, such as an active restriction, outranks
          it.</p>
          <p>Writes carry the value as a query parameter (OpModeLoadCmd=..., RestrictPower=&lt;JSON&gt;):
          sgr-commhandler up to 0.5.2 never sends the requestBody of a REST write call. A JSON
          body with the same field is accepted too.</p>
          <p>Evidence: GET /api/sgr/evidence/status and /api/sgr/evidence/events?after_seq=N
          (same credentials) return declared parameters and the journal of commands, decisions and
          device commands, correlated by id.</p>
        ]]>
      </textElement>
      <language>en</language>
    </programmerHints>
  </deviceInformation>
